%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 6f37df8d20f74e62a3e88f7fa41df9b0, type: 3}
  m_Name: Generic Bridge Lesson
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  panelTitle: BRIDGE BEHAVIOR
  minimumMessageDuration: 3.5
  fadeDuration: 0.2
  slideDistance: 24
  enableSlowMotion: 1
  simulationTimeScale: 0.5
  vehicleEnteredProgress: 0.1
  vehicleMidpointProgress: 0.5
  highStressThreshold: 0.7
  vehicleStuckDelay: 5
  simulationStarted: Simulation started. Watch the vehicle approach the bridge. Its live load will begin transferring only when its wheels reach the roadway.
  liveLoadStarted: The moving live load is transferring weight through the road, structural members, and supports into the ground.
  vehicleEnteredBridge: The live load has entered the bridge. Observe which members begin carrying more force.
  vehicleReachedMidpoint: The live load is near midspan, where the bridge is often farthest from its supports and structural demand can increase.
  highStressDetected: Orange or red members are using a high percentage of their capacity. Check whether the load has a direct, well-supported path to the anchors.
  stressLimitExceeded: The bridge exceeded the contract's allowed stress. Improve the load path, shorten unsupported spans, or add effective support.
  firstMemberBreak: A structural member exceeded its capacity and failed. The remaining structure must now carry the redistributed load.
  vehicleStuck: The vehicle has stopped moving. Check the road alignment, clearance, and excessive bridge deformation near its position.
  vehicleFailed: The continuous load path was lost before the vehicle completed the crossing. Strengthen the failed area and test again.
  bridgeSucceeded: The bridge carried the required live load successfully and maintained a continuous load path between its supports.
  simulationStopped: Simulation stopped. Review the bridge's movement and stressed areas before revising the design.
